## 1. Why Accuracy Alone Isn't Enough

This is the SINGLE most important lesson in classification evaluation. Consider this scenario:

```
A disease testing model checks 1000 patients.
990 are healthy, 10 actually have the disease.

If the model just predicts "Healthy" for EVERYONE, no matter what:
→ Accuracy = 990/1000 = 99%!

But it caught ZERO actual disease cases. It's a USELESS model
that just happens to have a great-looking accuracy number.
```

> ⚠️ This is exactly the "Imbalanced Dataset" problem coming up next in your roadmap. Accuracy lies when one class massively outnumbers the other — which is common in real-world data (fraud, disease, defects).

**This is why we need more metrics** — Precision, Recall, F1 — each tells a different part of the story.

