## 9. The Full Report in One Line

Scikit-learn has a shortcut that gives Precision, Recall, and F1 for EVERY class at once.

**Syntax:**
```python
from sklearn.metrics import classification_report

print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred))
```

```python
from sklearn.metrics import classification_report

print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred))
```
```
              precision    recall  f1-score   support

           0       0.75      0.75      0.75         4
           1       0.75      0.75      0.75         4

    accuracy                           0.75         8
   macro avg       0.75      0.75      0.75         8
weighted avg       0.75      0.75      0.75         8
```

> 💡 **This single function is what you'll use most often in real projects** — instead of calling 4 separate functions, `classification_report()` gives everything at once.

